  115: ## Getting started
  116: 
  117: Requirements: Node.js 24 recommended (the scripts execute TypeScript directly)
  118: and a modern browser. On Windows PowerShell, use `npm.cmd` if execution policy
  119: blocks `npm.ps1`.
  120: 
  121: ```bash
  122: npm install
  123: npm run dev        # web app on http://localhost:5173 + api on :8787
  124: npm run build      # production build into dist/
  125: npm run preview    # static UI; document parsing and live board collection need the API
  126: npm run typecheck  # tsc --noEmit
  127: ```
  128: 
  129: Live model calls are optional. The API uses `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`; consult
  130: `.env.example` and confirm an available model before enabling it. Intake can
  131: request structured interpretation; other calls primarily provide streamed text
  132: alongside deterministic drafts. Without a key, local interpretation and fixtures
  133: remain available. The Cohort and Curriculum components run deterministic code.
  134: The complete document walkthrough needs `npm run dev`, but no model key.
  135: 
  136: ## Proofs
  137: 
  138: The maths, the flows, and the intake pipeline are covered by deterministic
  139: proof scripts (no UI, no network):
  140: 
  141: ```bash
  142: npm run prove          # the spine and the canonical numbers (12 checks)
  143: npm run prove:backtest # the closed-loop backtest (4 checks)
  144: npm run prove:flow     # store, roles, state machine, analogy, closed loop (28 checks)
  145: npm run prove:signal   # the staged Signal reveal (12 checks)
  146: npm run prove:intake   # every demo file parses, interprets, files (18 checks)
  147: npm run prove:integrity # evidence edge cases and direct approval/rejection permissions (13 tests)
  148: npm run prove:teaching # course scope, validation, preparation counts and export (10 tests)
  149: npm run prove:curriculum # curriculum decisions, constraint checks, recovery and stale assessments (28 tests)
  150: npm run prove:evidence # evidence receipts, citations, denominators, Wilson intervals, mappings and backups (13 tests)
  151: npm run prove:collect  # board collectors: text extraction, normalisation, cache, rate limits, size and timeout (6 tests)
  152: npm run prove:research # research run: import on request, exact proposals, bulk review, briefs and notifications (5 tests)
  153: npm run prove:slides   # editable teaching packs and brief decks, unzipped and read back (3 tests)
  154: npm run prove:all      # 152 checks total
  155: ```
  156: 
  157: Headless verification of the built app:
