 114: 
 115: ## Getting started
 116: 
 117: Requirements: Node.js 24 recommended (the scripts execute TypeScript directly)
 118: and a modern browser. On Windows PowerShell, use `npm.cmd` if execution policy
 119: blocks `npm.ps1`.
 120: 
 121: ```bash
 122: npm install
 123: npm run dev        # web app on http://localhost:5173 + api on :8787
 124: npm run build      # production build into dist/
 125: npm run preview    # static UI; document parsing and live board collection need the API
 126: npm run typecheck  # tsc --noEmit
 127: ```
 128: 
 129: Live model calls are optional. The API uses `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`; consult
 130: `.env.example` and confirm an available model before enabling it. Intake can
 131: request structured interpretation; other calls primarily provide streamed text
 132: alongside deterministic drafts. Without a key, local interpretation and fixtures
 133: remain available. The Cohort and Curriculum components run deterministic code.
 134: The complete document walkthrough needs `npm run dev`, but no model key.
 135: 
 136: ## Proofs
 137: 
 138: The maths, the flows, and the intake pipeline are covered by deterministic
 139: proof scripts (no UI, no network):
 140: 
 141: ```bash
 142: npm run prove          # the spine and the canonical numbers (12 checks)
 143: npm run prove:backtest # the closed-loop backtest (4 checks)
 144: npm run prove:flow     # store, roles, state machine, analogy, closed loop (28 checks)
 145: npm run prove:signal   # the staged Signal reveal (12 checks)
 146: npm run prove:intake   # every demo file parses, interprets, files (18 checks)
 147: npm run prove:integrity # evidence edge cases and direct approval/rejection permissions (13 tests)
 148: npm run prove:teaching # course scope, validation, preparation counts and export (10 tests)
 149: npm run prove:curriculum # curriculum decisions, constraint checks, recovery and stale assessments (28 tests)
 150: npm run prove:evidence # evidence receipts, citations, denominators, Wilson intervals, mappings and backups (13 tests)
 151: npm run prove:collect  # board collectors: text extraction, normalisation, cache, rate limits, size and timeout (6 tests)
 152: npm run prove:research # research run: import on request, exact proposals, bulk review, briefs and notifications (5 tests)
 153: npm run prove:slides   # editable teaching packs and brief decks, unzipped and read back (3 tests)
 154: npm run prove:all      # 152 checks total
 155: ```
 156: 
 157: Headless verification of the built app:
 158: 
 159: ```bash
 160: npm run build
 161: node scripts/walk.mjs  # sign in, visit every screen, file a real upload, assert no errors
 162: npm run smoke          # play the full-tour demo, assert the end state including both downloaded decks
 163: npm run smoke:integrity # check fixture notices and the split-source warning; local browser only
 164: npm run smoke:workspace # lecturer save/reload/export, guides, keyboard and mobile checks
 165: npm run smoke:curriculum # create/revise/version, evidence receipts and report, real downloads and restore, 320/390px checks
 166: node scripts/generate-guide.mjs --check # in-app catalogue and Markdown guide agree
 167: ```
 168: 
 169: ## For judges
 170: 
 171: **[JUDGES.md](JUDGES.md)** explains the prototype walkthrough and its limitations.
 172: The current [as-built report, 9 October 2026](docs/lyceum-v3-as-built-2026-10-09.md) describes
 173: the build as verified. The historical [as-built document](docs/history/lyceum-v3-as-built.md) contains claims that the
 174: current [audit and improvement plan](docs/lyceum-improvement-plan.md) corrects.
 175: 
 176: ## The self-driving demo
 177: 
 178: The **Play demo** control on the sign-in screen, the public index and **Guide &
 179: progress** plays a full tour of one course over the real app with a simulated
 180: cursor, about five and a half minutes after three intro cards: a course revision under
 181: constraint checks with its version history, a research run on a dated saved
 182: sample of real postings, exact quotations with a rejected paraphrase, bulk
 183: review, a coverage mapping, a teaching session with its slide pack downloaded, a
 184: template assessment, a meeting brief with slides sent to the programme owner,
 185: the guide and backup page, and the recipient reading the brief. The counts,
 186: quotations, decks and brief are computed live; only the postings are a saved
 187: sample, labelled as such. Live board collection needs the local API and a
 188: network connection. Press record, click Play once. Sample decks can be
 189: generated with `node scripts/gen-sample-decks.mjs`. Regenerate the sample
 190: postings from a raw board download with
 191: `npm run gen:sample <board.json> <board> <retrievedAt>`.
 192: 
 193: ## Project structure
 194: 
 195: ```text
 196: server/               the thin api: /api/parse (5 formats), /api/collect (two permitted board APIs, cached and rate limited), /api/agent (streaming, fallback)
 197: public/demo/          real sample files: results.xlsx, clo-survey.csv, syllabus.pdf, lecture-slides.pptx, collected-sample.json (dated postings)
 198: src/
 199:   types.ts            the Layer 0 data contract
 200:   theme/              tokens + global styles (one system, no ad-hoc styling)
 201:   lib/                curriculum constraints/diffs/exports, teaching plans, evidence receipts and calculations, board collection, slide packs, validated workspace backups
 202:   lib/spine/          the illustrative Rasch spine (pure maths, reused from v2 byte-identical)
 203:   data/               seed, cohorts, items, the multi-source market snapshots
 204:   agents/             the seven agents: client wrappers, local interpreters, fixtures
 205:   app/                store (persistent), roles, staged simulations
 206:   ui/                 primitives, shell, course creation/revision, recovery and other screens
 207:   demo/               the self-driving demo: the research-run script, runner and overlay
 208: scripts/              generators and headless verification
 209: ```
